[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "adr-2809051000-ayatori-coscientist-iteration-02-async-block-source"
  :adr/title "ayatori co-scientist iteration 02: the async getter serves the pack, and a Worker stops paying discovery for blocks it holds"
  :adr/status "accepted"
  :adr/date "2026-09-05"
  :adr/related ["adr-2809041800-ayatori-coscientist-iteration-01-round-trips"
                "ADR-2608160100" "ADR-2606141500"]
  :adr/context
  "Iteration 01 landed :block-source on the SYNCHRONOUS getter only and left four seeds (bench/coscientist-iteration-01.edn). The first seed is the async path: open-snapshot-async still paid one IPNI discovery per block behind a pack, because the Worker-native getter had no source seam. A Worker serving its own pack therefore paid N wasted round trips per query -- the same waste H1 removed from the sync path."

  :adr/decision
  "provider-block-getter-async now takes :block-source. Contract identical to the sync getter: served BEFORE discovery, awaited if it returns a Promise, CID-verified on the same path as a provider answer, coalesced through :in-flight. A nil answer or a corrupt answer falls through to discovery -- the fall-through reuses the SAME provider loop (extracted as attempt-providers-async, so the two paths cannot drift) and is COUNTED as :source-failures so a corrupt pack is visible rather than merely slow. open-snapshot-async forwards the option. Absent :block-source, behaviour is byte-identical to before.

  bench/fitness.cljs adds a THIRD arm, packed-async: the same pack through open-snapshot-async. The harness now refuses unless all three arms answer the same 3 rows AND the async arm pays zero discoveries -- a cheaper arm cannot win by returning less, and the seed's claim is asserted, not narrated."

  :adr/consequences
  "Measured at 800 subjects: packed-async 8 round trips, 0 discoveries, 110,996 bytes -- parity transfer with the sync pack path and 1.50x fewer round trips than per-object. The metric the seed predicted is now measured, and the harness would have caught a silent regression: removing the source makes the async arm die with :ayatori/all-providers-failed, which the REFUSING path surfaces. nbb 101 tests / 315 assertions, 0 failures.

  Landed as kotoba-lang/ayatori PR #18, merged 61f9f04a. West pin advanced b577813c -> 61f9f04a; kagami reconcile absorbed it into the fleet-db ledger.

  Remaining seeds (unchanged in priority): bytes still come from an in-memory range server, so the byte figures are not a network measurement; the multi-pack regime is unmeasured; and packing POLICY (the write side) is untouched -- nothing in production writes a pack yet."
}]
